{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["For their vine is from the vine of Sodom — that is to say: why did I say, אַפְאִיהֶם אַשְׁבִּיתָה מֵאֱנוֹשׁ זָכְרָם? It was because of the arrogance of the nations, who are from the vine of Sodom; they deserved to drink the verdict that no remnant of them survive, just like Sodom and Amorah, for they sinned like Sodom and Amorah, as written: וְחַטַּאתְכֶם כִּסְדֹם הַגִּידוּ. The princes of Sodom, the people of Amorah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The final sentence 'קציני סדום עם עמורה' appears to be a secondary marginal gloss quoting Isaiah 1:10 appended to the comment; translated as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:55.077746187Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}